  {
    "sha": "35e6c8a1203599f28e20b55dd781a8de078c454b",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOMngV7toAKDM1ZTZjOGExMjAzNTk5ZjI4ZTIwYjU1ZGQ3ODFhOGRlMDc4YzQ1NGI",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Afonso Oliveira",
        "email": "afonso.oliveira707@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-02-02T16:53:50Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Afonso Oliveira",
        "email": "Afonso.Oliveira@synopsys.com",
        "date": "2026-02-02T17:10:16Z"
      },
      "message": "Add MMR (memory-mapped register) support to UDB tooling and PDF generation\n\nIntroduce a new database object type for memory-mapped registers (MMRs),\nwhich are accessed via physical addresses rather than the CSR address space.\nMMRs reuse CSR field definitions but have physical_address instead of a\n12-bit CSR address.\n\nChanges:\n- Add mmr_schema.json for YAML validation of MMR definitions\n- Add Mmr Ruby class with wavedrom_desc, exists_in_cfg?, optional_in_cfg?\n- Widen CsrField type signatures to accept T.any(Csr, Mmr) as parent\n- Register Mmr kind in DatabaseObject::Kind enum\n- Add MMR loading to Architecture and Extension classes\n- Handle mmr/mmr_field link types in resolve_links\n- Add MMR sections to ext_pdf AsciiDoc template and partial\n\nSigned-off-by: Afonso Oliveira <afonso.oliveira707@gmail.com>",
