        "email": "Afonso.Oliveira@synopsys.com",
        "date": "2026-02-02T17:10:16Z"
      },
      "message": "Add instruction definitions for Xaifoundry extensions\n\nDefine 238 instructions across 7 sub-extensions per the ET\nProgrammer's Reference Manual:\n\n- Xaifoundryamo (82): Global/local atomic operations (add, and, or,\n  xor, swap, min, max, cmpswap) for word/doubleword with both integer\n  and FP variants, plus scatter/gather memory operations\n- Xaifoundrycache (9): Cache management pseudo-instructions encoded as\n  CSRRW to ucache_control (flush, invalidate, flushinvalidate, lock,\n  locksw, lockva, evictsw, evictva, prefetchva)\n- Xaifoundryflb (1): Fast local barrier via CSRRW to flbarrier CSR\n- Xaifoundrymask (9): Mask register operations (and, or, xor, not,\n  popc, popz, mov between mask and integer registers)\n- Xaifoundrypi (37): Packed integer SIMD operations (arithmetic,\n  logical, shifts, comparisons, saturate, pack/replicate)\n- Xaifoundryps (81): Packed single-precision FP operations (arithmetic,\n  compare, convert, transcendental, swizzle, scatter/gather, cube map)\n- Xaifoundrytensor (19): Tensor operations (load, store, FMA, reduce,\n  broadcast, quantize, send/recv, wait)\n\nSigned-off-by: Afonso Oliveira <afonso.oliveira707@gmail.com>",
